WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
On the left, manual API and interface
runs compete for shared backend services,

00:00:04.064 --> 00:00:07.400
PostgreSQL accounts
and limited vendor test slots.

00:00:07.473 --> 00:00:10.320
There is no backend
service virtualization.

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:13.120
Engineers collect logs
and screenshots manually.

00:00:13.653 --> 00:00:17.840
On the right, an approved test commit
enters a pinned continuous integration

00:00:17.886 --> 00:00:22.080
runner. The pilot provisions a payment
service and datastore for each run,

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:26.320
resets synthetic balances,
and uses versioned WireMock behavior

00:00:26.507 --> 00:00:31.680
to reproduce provider faults. JUnit
and REST Assured check the transfer,

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:35.760
journal and balances.
An idempotency scenario verifies that

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:39.600
a retried payment creates one
transfer and one balanced journal.

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:44.560
Raw assertions, application logs
and run identifiers survive cleanup.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:49.280
AI assists drafting and evidence
interpretation under review.

00:00:49.387 --> 00:00:53.760
Isolated execution and controlled
dependencies come from quality engineering

00:00:53.817 --> 00:00:58.720
modernization. Real provider and
settlement checks remain separate gates.
